   "text": "I read the image as the decapeptide pGlu\u2011His\u2011Trp\u2011Ser\u2011Tyr\u2011D\u2011Trp\u2011Leu\u2011Arg\u2011Pro\u2011NHEt. This matches the GnRH analogue deslorelin, though I worked it out from the drawing rather than by recognising the name.\n\n**Residues, N\u2011terminus to C\u2011terminus:**\n- **pGlu:** a 5\u2011oxopyrrolidine ring whose carbonyl carbon is attached to His.\n- **His:** an imidazole side chain on a CH2.\n- **Trp (upper):** an indole side chain.\n- **Ser:** a CH2OH side chain.\n- **Tyr:** a 4\u2011hydroxyphenyl side chain.\n- **Trp (lower):** an indole side chain.\n- **Leu:** an isobutyl side chain.\n- **Arg:** a guanidine\u2011terminated propyl side chain.\n- **Pro:** a pyrrolidine ring, capped at the C\u2011terminus as an N\u2011ethyl amide (C(=O)NHCH2CH3).\n\n**Stereochemistry:** I assigned each \u03b1\u2011carbon from the wedge or hash on its carbonyl bond and the positions of its three drawn neighbours, with the implicit H on the opposite face.\n- pGlu, His, upper Trp, Ser, Tyr, Leu, Arg and Pro all come out S, i.e. the L configuration.\n- The lower Trp comes out R, i.e. D\u2011Trp.\n\nI wrote the SMILES from the C\u2011terminal ethylamide back toward pGlu. In that direction an L residue is written `[C@H]` and a D residue `[C@@H]`.\n\nSMILES: CCNC(=O)[C@@H]1CCCN1C(=O)[C@H](CCCN=C(N)N)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(C)C)NC(=O)[C@@H](Cc1c[nH]c2ccccc12)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1ccc(O)cc1)NC(=O)[C@H](CO)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1c[nH]c2ccccc12)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1c[nH]cn1)NC(=O)[C@@H]1CCC(=O)N1"
